    "body": "## Purpose\n\nPart of #62051 (the truncated/unclosed-parameter rows only; the block with no invoke, the cut inside a tool name, and the V4 spellings are not addressed here, so the issue should stay open) and extends the `arg_value_extender` incremental streaming architecture (introduced for `qwen3_xml` in #62027 and `minimax_m2` in #62035) to the DeepSeek DSML parsers (`deepseek_v32`, `deepseek_v4`, and `deepseek_v41`).\n\n### Problem (#62051)\n1. **Unclosed / Truncated DSML Parameters Produce Invalid JSON on Stream Flush**:\n   - In `_dsml_args_to_json(raw_args, partial)`, trailing unclosed `<\uff5cDSML\uff5cparameter name=\"...\" string=\"...\">...` tags were matched via `_PARTIAL_PARAM_RE` **only when `partial=True`**.\n   - When `partial=False` (called during `extract_tool_calls(...)` or during `_flush_arg_converter()` at `</\uff5cDSML\uff5cinvoke>` / `finish_streaming()`), `_PARTIAL_PARAM_RE` was skipped.\n   - As a result:\n     - **Case 1 (Truncated at `max_tokens`)**: During streaming, `converter(raw_args, True)` emitted `{\"url\": \"https://example.com` (`prev_converted_len > 0`). On `finish_streaming()`, `_flush_arg_converter()` called `converter(raw_args, False)` which returned `\"{}\"` (length 2 < `prev_converted_len`), so no closing `\"}` delta was emitted\u2014leaving clients with invalid, unclosed JSON (`{\"url\": \"https://example.com`).\n     - **Case 4 (Model omits `</\uff5cDSML\uff5cparameter>` before `</\uff5cDSML\uff5cinvoke>`)**: Non-streaming `extract_tool_calls` dropped the parameter (`{}`), while streaming emitted unclosed JSON (`{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/a`).\n2. **Quadratic Re-conversion of Long DSML Tool Arguments**:\n   - Unlike `Qwen3Parser` (#62027) and `MinimaxM2Parser` (#62035), DeepSeek DSML parsers lacked an `arg_value_extender` and re-ran full regex conversion over `slot.args` whenever `>` appeared inside streamed argument content (e.g., code, HTML, shell redirects, markdown).\n\n### Solution\n1. **Consistent Unclosed Parameter Recovery + Partial Tag Holdback**:\n   - Extract `_dsml_parse_args` so trailing unclosed `<\uff5cDSML\uff5cparameter ...>` blocks at the end of `raw_args` are recovered in both `partial=True` and `partial=False`.\n   - Add `_value_end_window(text, value_end_re)` using `regex.fullmatch(..., partial=True)` against `</\uff5cDSML\uff5cparameter>|<\uff5cDSML\uff5cparameter\\s+name=` so any trailing suffix of an open parameter value that could still complete into a closing or sibling parameter tag is held back during `partial=True` streaming (since `DeepSeekV4Parser` has no lexer transitions on `PARAM_START`/`PARAM_CLOSE` in `TOOL_ARGS`).\n   - Hold back `_unwrap_wrapper_args` when `partial=True` and a single `arguments`/`input` wrapper parameter contains an incomplete JSON string, preventing premature streaming of `\"arguments\": ` before unwrapping.\n2. **Incremental DSML String Argument Streaming (`_dsml_arg_value_extender`)**:\n   - Implement `_dsml_arg_value_extender` for `deepseek_v4`, `deepseek_v41`, and `deepseek_v32`, streaming open `string=\"true\"` DSML parameter values in $O(1)$ conversions with respect to argument length (reducing partial converter calls on a 200-line `write_file` call from 206 to 6).\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Added `TestArgValueExtender` in `tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py` (long 200-line DSML call with `>`, `<`, quotes, backslashes, and partial DSML tag lookalikes; $O(1)$ conversion count verification; #62051 truncated & unclosed parameter streaming/non-streaming parity).\n- Added parametrized streaming and non-streaming tests for truncated and unclosed parameters in `tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41.py` and `tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v32.py`.\n- All 279 tests in `tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v32.py`, `test_deepseek_v4.py`, `test_deepseek_v41.py`, and `test_parser_engine.py` pass.\n\n### Credits & Acknowledgments\n- Credit to **@robertgshaw2-redhat** for reporting #62051 and providing the DSML truncation/unclosed-parameter reproduction cases, and to **@YaashuDave** for reproducing all five cases and analyzing `StreamingParserEngine.finish()` on #62051.\n- Credit to **@deadstrobe5** (#62027, #62035) for designing the `ArgValueExtender` incremental argument streaming architecture in `ParserEngine`, and **@jayzuccarelli** (#58780) for prior work on incremental DeepSeek V3.2/V4 tool argument streaming.\n- Special thanks to **@JohnZhao01** (#62290) and **@smiyamoto3** for end-to-end validation, edge-case reproductions, and review feedback on this PR.\n",
